   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public housing law, in relation to establishing the lease and landlord fraud public awareness program to promote public awareness of the potential risks of signing a fraudulent lease with an individual misrepresenting themselves as a landlord",
    "basePrintNo": "S631",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S631-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 8,
       "fullName": "John E. Brooks",
       "imgName": "923_John_Brooks.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1101,
       "sessionMemberId": 1097,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "BROOKS"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §20-a, Pub Hous L",
    "lawSection": "Public Housing Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S631\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public housing law, in relation to establishing\nthe lease and landlord fraud public awareness program to promote\npublic awareness of the potential risks of signing a fraudulent lease\nwith an individual misrepresenting themselves as a landlord\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis bill will create a public awareness program to inform the public\nof the risks of signing a fraudulent or invalid lease.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Amends the public housing law to create a public awareness\nprogram.\n\nSection 2. Effective Date\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nDue to the recent housing crisis, many homes have been foreclosed or\nbecome abandoned homes. This has allowed for unscrupulous individuals\nto prey on those looking for housing to rent these homes as if they\nwere their own. An individual signing into a false lease often end up\nlosing their home, their rent payment and their security deposit.\nThese deceived individuals are frequently then subject to town code\nviolations.\n\nA public awareness program will assist individuals who could be\ndeceived into renting a house or apartment from individuals\nmisrepresenting themselves as landlords. This bill will require the\nDivision of Housing and Community Renewal to create a public awareness\ncampaign to warn would-be renters about lease and landlord fraud.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016: Passed Senate, referred to Assembly Housing\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the 180 day after it shall have become a\nlaw.\n",
