    "lawCode": "Amd §94-a, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S631A\n\nSPONSOR: BOYLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to\nestablishing the lease and landlord fraud public awareness program to\npromote public awareness of the potential risks of signing a fraudulent\nlease with an individual misrepresenting themselves as a landlord\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill will create a public awareness program to inform the public of\nthe risks of signing a fraudulent or invalid lease.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends the executive law to create a public awareness\nprogram.\n\nSection 2. Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDue to the recent housing crisis, many homes have been foreclosed or\nbecome abandoned homes. This has allowed for unscrupulous individuals to\nprey on those looking for housing to rent these homes as if they were\ntheir own. An individual signing into a false lease often end up losing\ntheir home, their rent payment and their security deposit.  These\ndeceived individuals are frequently then subject to town code\nviolations.\n\nA public awareness program will assist individuals who could be deceived\ninto renting a house or apartment from individuals misrepresenting them-\nselves as landlords. This bill will require the Division of Housing and\nCommunity Renewal to create a public awareness campaign to warn would-be\nrenters about lease and landlord fraud.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2016: Passed Senate, referred to Assembly Housing\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the 180 day after it shall have become a\nlaw.\n",
